  {
   "id": 517149,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/abe1113bd9fc052d.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Steven Novella/NeuroLogica)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>Humans have 46 chromosomes. Great apes, including orangutans, gorillas and chimpanzees have 48 chromosomes. The image compares the human chromosomes 1 to 4 with great ape chromosomes 1 to 5.</p>\n<p>Make a hypothesıs based on this image.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1011446,
     "content_html": "The common ancestor of great apes and humans had 46 chromosomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1011447,
     "content_html": "The common ancestor of great apes and humans had 48 chromosomes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1011448,
     "content_html": "Of the three great apes, humans are most closely related to gorillas."
    },
    {
     "id": 1011449,
     "content_html": "Of the three great apes, humans are most closely related to orangutans."
    }
   ],
